  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -734,7 +734,7 @@ on using the <<ChToolsDebugger, Debugger Tools>>.\n To build the Wireshark User's Guide and the Wireshark Developer's Guide,\n build the `all_guides` target, e.g.  `msbuild all_guides.vcxproj`.\n Detailed information to build these guides can be found in the file\n-_doc\\README.adoc_ in the Wireshark sources.\n+_doc\\README.documentation.adoc_ in the Wireshark sources.\n \n ==== Optional: Create a Wireshark Installer\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/wsdg_src/wsdg_quick_setup.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/wsdg_src/wsdg_quick_setup.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -90,5 +90,4 @@ _attributes.adoc_. The User’s Guide and Developer’s Guide are split\n across several files, and only the top-level _user-guide.adoc_ and\n _developer-guide.adoc_ include _attributes.adoc_. As a result,\n some markup will be incomplete. You can work around this somewhat by\n-adding some attributes such as `compat-mode experimental` to your Live\n-Preview settings.\n+adding the `experimental` attribute to your Live Preview settings.\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/README.documentation.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/README.documentation.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -44,8 +44,7 @@ Lua tables. (you can do so, but it's not advisable)\n Both of the scripts above are given the C-source files to search through\n by the make process, generated from the lists in epan/wslua/CMakeLists.txt.\n Naturally if you add new source files, you need to add them to the list in\n-epan/wslua/CMakeLists.txt. You also have to add the module name into\n-doc/user-guide.xml and doc/wsluarm.xml, and the source files into\n+epan/wslua/CMakeLists.txt. You also have to add the source files into\n doc/CMakeLists.txt, to get it to be generated in the user guide.\n \n Due to those documentation and registration scripts, you MUST follow some very\n@@ -284,9 +283,8 @@ file as that WSLUA_MODULE comment.  You'll also note the documentation\n includes a sub-section for 'Non Method Functions', which it auto-generated\n from anything with a 'WSLUA_FUNCTION' macro (as opposed to class member\n functions, which use the 'WSLUA_METHOD' and 'WSLUA_CONSTRUCTOR' macros). Also,\n-to make new wslua files generate documentation, it is not sufficient to just\n-add this macro to a new file and add the file to the CMakeLists.txt; you also\n-have to add the module name into doc/user-guide.xml, and doc/wsluarm.xml.\n+to make new wslua files generate documentation, add this macro to a new file\n+and add the file to the doc/CMakeLists.txt.\n \n \n WSLUA_CONTINUE_MODULE - like WSLUA_MODULE, except used at the top of a .c file\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/README.wslua",
      "old_path": "doc/README.wslua",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    }
